<%#
  Local override of studio-engine's modal host. Divergences from the
  gem partial:
    1. Card-level transition classes — thematic spring/slide keyframes
       (defined in app/assets/tailwind/application.css) instead of the engine's
       plain `transition ease-out duration-200`.
    2. swap() / advance() directional in-flow slide for multi-step flows.
    3. A per-modal entrance/exit animation registry (window.ModalAnimations
       + modalAnim()): open a modal with { enterAnim: 'shake' } / { exitAnim:
       'slide' } to pick a named animation. 'pop' (spring bounce/fall) is the
       default. Add an animation = one registry entry + one CSS class; re-skin
       a modal's entrance = change the key it's opened with. See showTokensPanel
       in contests/_turf_totals_board.html.erb for the 'shake' ("not quite
       yet") usage on the Get Entry Tokens modal.
  Backdrop fade + scroll lock + escape + click-outside + ARIA all stay
  identical to the engine so future engine bug fixes can be cherry-picked.

  studio-engine 0.20 now ships a reconciled host carrying this machinery
  (ModalAnimations, swap/advance, holdAtLeast) PLUS two guards this copy
  lacks (the open() stale-entry guard and the cardClasses() set-key
  guard). This override is intentionally KEPT for now — it also registers
  the turf cosign-rejected modal inline, which the engine host does not.
  Reconciling the two (adopt the engine host + a configurable transition-
  class set + an app modal-registration hook) is a dedicated follow-up.
%>
<%# body.modal-open + @keyframes studio-modal-drain live in
    app/assets/tailwind/application.css (migrated 2026-05-24). %>
<script>
  (function() {
    // === StudioModals helpers ===========================================
    window.StudioModals = window.StudioModals || {};
    window.StudioModals.holdAtLeast = function(minMs) {
      var startedAt = Date.now();
      return {
        then: function(callback) {
          var remaining = Math.max(0, minMs - (Date.now() - startedAt));
          if (remaining === 0) { callback(); return; }
          setTimeout(callback, remaining);
        }
      };
    };

    // === Modal card width registry =====================================
    //
    // The card is max-w-sm by default, which is right for a question and two
    // buttons. A modal carrying something with an INTRINSIC aspect ratio needs
    // more: wallet-setup shows a 16:9 explainer video, and at max-w-sm the
    // player is small enough that the thing it is teaching cannot be read.
    //
    // Keyed by modal id, NOT passed as a prop, on purpose. wallet-setup is
    // opened from three places (the board's entry gate, the onboarding chain
    // driver, and the post-Connect reopen) and a prop would have to be
    // remembered at each — one miss and the same card is two different widths
    // depending on how the user arrived.
    window.StudioModals.CARD_WIDTHS = { 'wallet-setup': 'max-w-md' };
    window.StudioModals.DEFAULT_CARD_WIDTH = 'max-w-sm';

    // === Modal animation registry ======================================
    //
    // The single place to define + tune named entrance / exit animations
    // for the modal card. Each key maps to a CSS class (in
    // app/assets/tailwind/application.css) plus its duration in ms (the store waits
    // this long before splicing a closing entry off the stack, so the
    // exit keyframe plays to completion before the DOM unmounts).
    //
    // Pass a key into any open() call via props.enterAnim / props.exitAnim:
    //
    //   $store.modals.open('foo', { enterAnim: 'shake' })          // shake in, default pop out
    //   $store.modals.open('bar', { exitAnim: 'slide' })           // default pop in, slide out
    //
    // Omitted → the modal uses 'pop' (the spring bounce in / fall out
    // that every modal has shipped with). To add a new animation: add one
    // entry here + one matching CSS class. To re-skin a modal's entrance,
    // just change the enterAnim it's opened with — no host edits needed.
    //
    // NB: this is independent of the directional swap()/advance() slide,
    // which is a separate in-flow transition mechanism (see below) and
    // always uses the modal-card-swap-* classes regardless of these keys.
    window.ModalAnimations = window.ModalAnimations || {
      enter: {
        pop:   { cls: 'modal-card-mount',    ms: 320 },  // default — spring bounce in
        shake: { cls: 'modal-card-shake-in', ms: 600 },  // "not quite yet" Discord-style nope
        slide: { cls: 'modal-card-swap-in',  ms: 220 }   // slide in from the left
      },
      exit: {
        pop:   { cls: 'modal-card-unmount',  ms: 220 },  // default — anticipation + fall
        slide: { cls: 'modal-card-swap-out', ms: 220 }   // slide out to the right
      }
    };
    function modalAnim(channel, key) {
      var table = window.ModalAnimations[channel] || {};
      return table[key] || table.pop;
    }

    // === Alpine.store('modals') — the stack ============================
    //
    // CLOSE_ANIM_MS: keep in sync with the modal-card-unmount + modal-
    // backdrop-unmount keyframes in app/assets/tailwind/application.css. When
    // close() is called, we set _closing on the entry so the host
    // can swap in the unmount classes, then actually pop the stack
    // after this many ms so the animation plays before the DOM
    // unmounts. If you change the keyframe durations there, bump
    // this to match.
    var CLOSE_ANIM_MS = 220;
    var SWAP_IN_MS    = 220;

    document.addEventListener('alpine:init', function() {
      if (Alpine.store('modals')) return;
      // FOCUS STATE, kept in this closure and NOT on the store. A DOM node
      // assigned to a reactive store reads back as a Proxy, and every identity
      // check against it (===, contains) is false forever — the defect that made
      // the wallet watcher discard every account-change event it received.
      var _returnFocusTo = null;
      var _backdropEl = null;
      Alpine.store('modals', {
        stack: [],
        // open(id, props, opts)
        //   opts.replace: true  → swap the top entry with this one. When a
        //     non-closing modal is currently visible, the swap is a directional
        //     slide — current modal exits stage-right (modal-card-swap-out)
        //     and the new one enters stage-left (modal-card-swap-in). Gives
        //     a "forward progress" feel for wizards / multi-step flows.
        //     Defaults to a plain mount animation when the stack is empty.
        //   opts.replace: false (default) → push on top of the stack. Stacking
        //     semantics — when the new one closes, the previous is revealed
        //     underneath (e.g. crop-photo on top of profile).
        // SWAP_IN_MS must match the modal-card-swap-in animation duration in
        // app/assets/tailwind/application.css; we clear the flag after that so a fresh
        // open() doesn't re-trigger the slide.
        open: function(id, props, opts) {
          props = props || {};
          opts  = opts  || {};
          var self = this;

          if (opts.replace && this.stack.length > 0) {
            var current = this.current();
            if (current && !current._closing) {
              // Phase 1: mark leaving entry with _swappingOut + _closing so
              // the :class binding swaps in the slide-out keyframe (instead
              // of the default scale-pop modal-card-unmount) for CLOSE_ANIM_MS.
              // _swapDir picks which slide direction (forward = exit right,
              // back = exit left); the same flag carries onto the new entry
              // below so slide-in mirrors slide-out.
              var dir = (opts.direction === 'back') ? 'back' : 'forward';
              current._swapDir = dir;
              current._swappingOut = true;
              current._closing = true;
              setTimeout(function() {
                // Phase 2: stack swap. New entry carries _swappingIn + the
                // same _swapDir so the host's :class binding picks the
                // matching slide-in keyframe.
                var idx = self.stack.indexOf(current);
                var newEntry = { id: id, props: props, _swappingIn: true, _swapDir: dir };
                if (idx >= 0) {
                  self.stack[idx] = newEntry;
                } else {
                  self.stack.push(newEntry);
                }
                self._sync();
                // The content template just re-mounted and unfocused whatever was
                // focused; put focus back on the backdrop or the trap releases.
                self.refocus();
                // Phase 3: clear the swap-in flag + direction after the
                // slide finishes so a future close() runs the unmount
                // keyframe cleanly. _settled latches so the host's
                // :class binding doesn't snap modal-card-mount back on
                // (which would re-fire the bounce-in keyframe from
                // opacity:0 and look like a flash mid-settle).
                setTimeout(function() {
                  newEntry._swappingIn = false;
                  newEntry._swapDir = null;
                  newEntry._settled = true;
                }, SWAP_IN_MS);
              }, CLOSE_ANIM_MS);
              return;
            }
            // Already mid-close — just hot-swap so we don't double up timers.
            this.stack[this.stack.length - 1] = { id: id, props: props };
          } else {
            this.stack.push({ id: id, props: props });
          }
          this._sync();
        },

        // === FOCUS CONTRACT — ported from studio-engine's studio/modals/_host
        // (/tasks/consumers-fork-modal-host). This app SHADOWS the engine's host,
        // so a gem bump does NOT deliver these: the engine file is never rendered
        // here. Verified before porting — this fork carried none of them.
        captureFocus: function(el) {
          _returnFocusTo = document.activeElement;
          _backdropEl = el;
          // The backdrop itself, not the first control: landing on a button means
          // a stray Enter fires it, and a destructive card should not be one
          // keystroke from confirming.
          if (el && el.focus) el.focus();
        },

        // RE-FOCUS AFTER THE TOP ENTRY CHANGES, without re-capturing the return
        // target. captureFocus runs from x-init on the backdrop, and a swap keeps
        // current() truthy, so the outer template never re-mounts and x-init never
        // re-runs — while the inner content DOES re-mount and unmounts the focused
        // control. activeElement then falls to the document body, which is not
        // inside the backdrop, so the tab handler bound there stops firing and
        // native tabbing resumes. Re-capturing _returnFocusTo here would overwrite
        // the opener with a node inside the dialog.
        refocus: function() {
          var run = function() {
            if (_backdropEl && _backdropEl.focus && document.contains(_backdropEl)) {
              _backdropEl.focus();
            }
          };
          if (window.Alpine && window.Alpine.nextTick) window.Alpine.nextTick(run);
          else setTimeout(run, 0);
        },

        releaseFocus: function() {
          var target = _returnFocusTo;
          _returnFocusTo = null;
          _backdropEl = null;
          // Only restore if still in the document — a Turbo visit can replace the
          // page under an open modal, and focusing a detached node silently moves
          // focus to the document body, which is worse than leaving it alone.
          if (target && target.focus && document.contains(target)) target.focus();
        },

        // Recomputed per keypress on purpose: modal content is Alpine-rendered and
        // a card can add or remove controls (a spinner replacing a button) while
        // open, so a list captured at mount goes stale.
        focusables: function(el) {
          if (!el) return [];
          var sel = 'a[href], button:not([disabled]), input:not([disabled]), ' +
                    'select:not([disabled]), textarea:not([disabled]), [tabindex]';
          return Array.prototype.slice.call(el.querySelectorAll(sel)).filter(function(n) {
            return n.tabIndex >= 0 && n.offsetParent !== null;
          });
        },

        // Tab is intercepted (.prevent on the binding) and re-dispatched here.
        // That only holds while focus is INSIDE the backdrop — the binding lives
        // there and sees the key only when activeElement is a descendant, which is
        // why refocus() exists.
        cycleFocus: function(el, event) {
          var items = this.focusables(el);
          if (!items.length) { if (el && el.focus) el.focus(); return; }
          var i = items.indexOf(document.activeElement);
          var next = event.shiftKey ? (i <= 0 ? items.length - 1 : i - 1)
                                    : (i === items.length - 1 ? 0 : i + 1);
          items[next].focus();
        },

        // The dialog's accessible NAME. A CHAIN, not a pair of ifs: an empty
        // string must fall through, or the dialog announces as unnamed — worse
        // than the humanised id it was meant to improve on.
        dialogLabel: function() {
          var entry = this.current();
          if (!entry) return 'Dialog';
          var p = entry.props || {};
          return p.ariaLabel || p.title || String(entry.id).replace(/[-_]/g, ' ');
        },
        // Sugar — `swap('foo', props)` ≡ `open('foo', props, { replace: true })`.
        // Pass opts through so callers can request a back-direction slide
        // on a cross-modal handoff if the new modal is semantically
        // upstream of the current one (e.g. "return to home modal").
        swap: function(id, props, opts) {
          return this.open(id, props, Object.assign({ replace: true }, opts || {}));
        },
        // advance(propsPatch, opts) — patch the current entry's props
        // WITH the same directional slide as swap(), but WITHOUT
        // replacing the stack entry. Use this for in-flow step
        // transitions inside one modal (e.g. picker → waiting →
        // confirming) where the modal's outer x-data scope (form
        // state, watchers, factories) needs to survive the transition.
        // swap() drops a fresh entry into the stack which re-evaluates
        // the registered <template x-if="id===...">  — fine for
        // cross-modal handoffs, but heavy for "same modal, next step."
        // advance() is the lightweight cousin.
        //
        // opts.direction: 'forward' (default — current exits right, next
        //   enters from left; reads as "moving ahead in the flow")
        //   or 'back' (mirrored — current exits left, next enters from
        //   right; reads as "returning to the previous step"). Pair
        //   forward calls with back calls on their inverse buttons so
        //   the user's spatial model of the wizard stays consistent.
        //
        // Timing mirrors swap():
        //   t=0      → flip _swappingOut, outer card slides off (CLOSE_ANIM_MS)
        //   t=220ms  → patch props, flip _swappingIn, card slides in
        //   t=440ms  → clear _swappingIn + _swapDir so the next open/
        //              close uses default mount/unmount keyframes
        //
        // Guards: no-op if no current entry, or if the entry is already
        // closing or mid-swap (prevents double-clicks from stacking timers).
        advance: function(propsPatch, opts) {
          opts = opts || {};
          var cur = this.current();
          if (!cur || cur._closing || cur._swappingOut) return;
          var self = this;
          cur._swapDir = (opts.direction === 'back') ? 'back' : 'forward';
          cur._swappingOut = true;
          setTimeout(function() {
            // Re-resolve in case the stack mutated during the slide-out
            // window. If our entry got popped (e.g. user hit Escape mid-
            // animation), bail rather than splat props onto a stale ref.
            if (self.stack.indexOf(cur) < 0) return;
            if (propsPatch) Object.assign(cur.props, propsPatch);
            cur._swappingOut = false;
            cur._swappingIn = true;
            // Same re-mount, same release — advance() patches props in place, so
            // the outer template never re-runs x-init either.
            self.refocus();
            setTimeout(function() {
              cur._swappingIn = false;
              cur._swapDir = null;
              cur._settled = true;
            }, SWAP_IN_MS);
          }, CLOSE_ANIM_MS);
        },
        close: function() {
          var self = this;
          var entry = this.current();
          if (!entry || entry._closing) return;  // empty stack or already closing
          // Flip _closing → Alpine reactivity adds the modal-card-unmount
          // and modal-backdrop-unmount classes via the :class bindings on
          // the host. Wait CLOSE_ANIM_MS for the animation to play, then
          // splice THIS specific entry from the stack (not pop() — the
          // top might have changed if another open() ran during the
          // close window). The splice delay tracks the entry's chosen
          // exit animation (props.exitAnim → registry ms) so a longer
          // custom exit keyframe plays fully before the DOM unmounts;
          // defaults to the 'pop' fall (220ms).
          entry._closing = true;
          setTimeout(function() {
            var idx = self.stack.indexOf(entry);
            if (idx >= 0) {
              self.stack.splice(idx, 1);
              self._sync();
            }
            // Only when the LAST dialog leaves. A stacked flow unmounts one and
            // reveals another, and returning focus to the ORIGINAL opener there
            // would yank the user out of the dialog still on screen.
            //
            // OUTSIDE the idx guard, matching the engine (_host.html.erb:494). Inside
            // it, the release is skipped whenever the entry is ALREADY GONE — press
            // Escape on a dismissible modal, then let clearStaleModals() ->
            // closeAllDismissible() fire from turbo:before-cache or a bfcache pageshow
            // inside the 220ms exit window: idx is -1, the block never runs, focus is
            // stranded on a detached backdrop, and _returnFocusTo / _backdropEl leak
            // into the next dialog. The stack length is the condition; whether THIS
            // call did the splicing is not.
            if (!self.stack.length) self.releaseFocus();
          }, modalAnim('exit', entry.props && entry.props.exitAnim).ms);
        },
        closeAll: function() {
          // No animation — used by Turbo before-cache + bfcache cleanup
          // where the user is navigating away and we just need the DOM
          // clean immediately.
          // TURBO/BFCACHE TEARDOWN: drop the return target rather than restore into a
          // document about to be replaced. Aligned with the engine (_host.html.erb:500).
          //
          // This fork used to CALL releaseFocus() here and justify it with "no-ops safely
          // if that node left the document". That misreads the timing:
          // `turbo:before-cache` fires while the node is STILL in the document, so the
          // call does not no-op — it moves focus onto a page the browser is one tick from
          // snapshotting and replacing.
          _returnFocusTo = null;
          this.stack = [];
          this._sync();
        },
        // Drops every modal whose props don't explicitly opt out of dismissal
        // (i.e. dismissible: false). Mirrors studio-engine v0.4.11. Used by
        // the bfcache + Turbo snapshot cleanup below so an in-flight on-chain
        // TX modal — which sets dismissible: false to forbid losing its UI
        // mid-flight — survives a back/forward navigation; the still-running
        // JS promise's solanaModal.success() resolves against a non-empty
        // stack. Celebratory modals (default dismissible: true) still clear.
        closeAllDismissible: function() {
          this.stack = this.stack.filter(function(modal) {
            return modal.props && modal.props.dismissible === false;
          });
          this._sync();
        },
        isOpen: function(id) {
          for (var i = 0; i < this.stack.length; i++) {
            if (this.stack[i].id === id) return true;
          }
          return false;
        },
        current: function() {
          return this.stack.length ? this.stack[this.stack.length - 1] : null;
        },
        // cardClasses() — the animation class set for the visible card.
        // Resolves the entry's enter/exit animation keys (props.enterAnim
        // / props.exitAnim) through the ModalAnimations registry, while
        // keeping the directional swap-* classes (the in-flow slide) as
        // fixed names. Lifecycle → class:
        //   fresh mount  → enter key class  (default 'pop' → modal-card-mount)
        //   closing      → exit key class   (default 'pop' → modal-card-unmount)
        //   swap/advance → modal-card-swap-{in,out}[-back]
        // The mount class is gated on !_settled (so a completed swap doesn't
        // re-fire the bounce) and !_closing (so close shows ONLY the exit
        // keyframe, not both stacked).
        cardClasses: function() {
          var c = this.current();
          if (!c) return {};
          var o = {};
          // Width comes from here rather than a static class on the element:
          // two competing max-w-* utilities would be resolved by stylesheet
          // source order, which is not something this file gets to decide.
          o[window.StudioModals.CARD_WIDTHS[c.id] ||
            window.StudioModals.DEFAULT_CARD_WIDTH] = true;
          if (!c._settled && !c._swappingIn && !c._swappingOut && !c._closing) {
            o[modalAnim('enter', c.props && c.props.enterAnim).cls] = true;
          }
          if (c._closing && !c._swappingOut) {
            o[modalAnim('exit', c.props && c.props.exitAnim).cls] = true;
          }
          o['modal-card-swap-in']       = !!(c._swappingIn  && c._swapDir !== 'back');
          o['modal-card-swap-out']      = !!(c._swappingOut && c._swapDir !== 'back');
          o['modal-card-swap-in-back']  = !!(c._swappingIn  && c._swapDir === 'back');
          o['modal-card-swap-out-back'] = !!(c._swappingOut && c._swapDir === 'back');
          return o;
        },
        _sync: function() {
          if (this.stack.length) {
            document.body.classList.add('modal-open');
          } else {
            document.body.classList.remove('modal-open');
          }
        }
      });
    });

    // === bfcache + Turbo snapshot cleanup ==============================
    // closeAllDismissible() keeps dismissible: false modals (pending
    // on-chain TX) so the user returning via bfcache doesn't silently lose
    // the modal that a still-in-flight JS promise will resolve against.
    function clearStaleModals() {
      if (window.Alpine && Alpine.store) {
        var m = Alpine.store('modals');
        if (m && typeof m.closeAllDismissible === 'function') {
          m.closeAllDismissible();
        } else if (m && typeof m.closeAll === 'function') {
          m.closeAll();
        }
      }
    }
    window.addEventListener('pageshow', function(e) { if (e.persisted) clearStaleModals(); });
    document.addEventListener('turbo:before-cache', clearStaleModals);
  })();
</script>

<template x-if="$store.modals.current()">
  <%# Backdrop + card use CSS @keyframe animations (NOT Alpine
      x-transition). On mount, the .modal-backdrop-mount + .modal-card-mount
      classes fire fade-in + drop-recoil. On close, the store flips
      _closing → the :class bindings add .modal-*-unmount → the exit
      keyframes play → 220ms later the store splices the entry from
      the stack and the whole thing unmounts (now invisible). %>
  <div class="fixed inset-0 z-[var(--z-modal)] flex items-center justify-center p-4 modal-backdrop-mount"
       :class="$store.modals.current()?._closing && 'modal-backdrop-unmount'"
       style="background:rgba(0,0,0,0.6)"
       role="dialog"
       aria-modal="true"
       <%# tabindex=-1 makes the backdrop programmatically focusable without
           adding it to the tab order, so captureFocus has somewhere to land that
           is not a button. x-init captures on mount; the trap intercepts Tab and
           re-dispatches it inside. :aria-label gives the dialog a NAME — an
           unnamed dialog announces as just "dialog" to a screen reader. %>
       tabindex="-1"
       x-init="$store.modals.captureFocus($el)"
       :aria-label="$store.modals.dialogLabel()"
       @keydown.tab.prevent="$store.modals.cycleFocus($el, $event)"
       @keydown.escape.window="$store.modals.current() && $store.modals.current().props.dismissible !== false && $store.modals.close()"
       @click.self="$store.modals.current() && $store.modals.current().props.dismissible !== false && $store.modals.close()">
    <%# Card animation is class-driven so it can pick the right keyframe
        for the current store state. Plain mount/unmount for first
        open + close. Swap-out + swap-in for inter-modal transitions
        triggered by $store.modals.swap() / advance() (or open with
        { replace: true }). _swapDir picks forward (exit right / enter
        left — default) vs back (exit left / enter right — opt-in via
        { direction: 'back' }).
        modal-card-mount is gated on !_settled so when a swap-in
        completes (which clears _swappingIn) the class binding does
        NOT snap back to modal-card-mount and re-fire the bounce-in
        keyframe — without the gate, the card briefly disappears and
        bounces in again right as the slide finishes, which reads as
        a flash mid-transition. _settled also stays true for the rest
        of the entry's lifetime so a stale Alpine re-evaluation can't
        retrigger the bounce. %>
    <%# No max-w-* here — cardClasses() supplies exactly one, per modal id.
        See the card width registry above. %>
    <%# max-h-[85dvh] + overflow-y-auto: the fourth engine focus fix, and the one
        this fork missed. The backdrop centres the card with `flex items-center`, so a
        card taller than the viewport is clipped past BOTH edges with nothing
        scrollable — its actions unreachable. On a dismissible: false card, escape and
        click-outside are deliberately gated off, so there is no way out at all.
        Trigger: a multi-field card on a landscape phone. It arrived in the engine in
        the SAME commit as captureFocus (4cb1720), which is why it belongs here rather
        than in a separate concern. dvh, not vh, so mobile browser chrome counts. %>
    <div class="bg-surface rounded-xl border border-subtle shadow-2xl p-6 w-full max-h-[85dvh] overflow-y-auto"
         :class="$store.modals.cardClasses()">
      <%= yield if block_given? %>
      <%# Audit C1 — cosign-rejected (tx mismatch) modal. Registered here in
          the shared host shell rather than in the per-app block passed to the
          host, so a SINGLE registration serves both render paths that route
          through this partial: the live layout (layouts/application) and the
          /admin gallery preview iframe (layouts/modal_preview). The app's other
          modals are registered per-layout in those blocks; this one sits in the
          shell intentionally. Opened with
          Alpine.store('modals').open('cosign-rejected', {}) from the entry
          boards when confirm_onchain_entry answers code 'tx_rejected'. current()
          is non-null here — gated by the outer template x-if above. %>
      <template x-if="$store.modals.current().id === 'cosign-rejected'">
        <%= render "modals/cosign_rejected" %>
      </template>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>
